## .chktexrc --- project-local ChkTeX configuration for Ego-research.
##
## LaTeX Workshop lints the open file with chktex and passes this file to it
## (`chktex ... -l <abs path to .chktexrc>`), so everything below governs what
## shows up in the editor's Problems panel.
##
## chktex is invoked with `-wall`, i.e. every message class is enabled.  For a
## technical document full of identifiers, file paths and inline math that
## produces mostly false positives and pure style advice, which drowns the few
## real findings.  `CmdLine` is chktex's mechanism for making command-line
## options permanent, so the noisy classes are muted here.
##
## Muted classes, and why each one is noise for this project:
##   8   dash length           hyphens inside identifiers, paths and ISO dates
##                             (2026.10.05-2026.10.11-openwam-libero,
##                             2026-10-05T18:40:58+08:00) and the deliberate
##                             en-dashes (world--action, vision--language--action)
##   9   unbalanced ( )        parentheses inside \texttt{...} Python snippets
##                             that are split across several groups
##   12  interword spacing     "sentence. \emph{...}"
##   13  intersentence \@      sentence-ending acronyms ("GPU. No ...", "et al.,")
##   21  command not intended  \, and friends inside $...$ (same origin as 46)
##   24  space before \label   \label on its own line after \section{...}
##   36  space before (        function calls inside \texttt{...}, e.g. env.reset()
##   41  primitive TeX         deliberate \vskip / \def in the two .sty files
##   46  \(...\) vs $...$       this project writes inline math as $...$
##
## The genuine findings were fixed in the sources, not muted: class 1 (command
## terminated by a space) everywhere except \egobgdir, class 2 (missing
## non-breaking space) and class 6 (missing italic correction).
##
## \egobgdir is the one exception: it ends the asset directory on the letter
## `r', so the Chinese file name that follows has to start with a space to
## terminate the control word, and graphicx cannot take the `{}' idiom (the
## braces would be spliced into the file name, e.g.
## `figures/beamer_background/{}页眉页脚.png').  `Silent' is chktex's list of
## commands for which a trailing space is legitimate; the entry below is
## appended to chktex's built-in list.

Silent
{
    \egobgdir
}

TabSize = 8

CmdLine
{
    -n8 -n9 -n12 -n13 -n21 -n24 -n36 -n41 -n46
}
